# Admin login.
#
# One or more accounts, as comma-separated `name:password` pairs:
#
#   ADMIN_USERS="chris:hunter2,steven:hunter3"
#
# Only the first colon in an entry separates the name from the password, so a
# password may contain colons. A password may NOT contain a comma, since that
# would split the entry in two. Names are matched case-insensitively and trimmed.
#
# Adding someone later is another pair here, followed by a redeploy.
#
# These are stored in plain text, the same way the single ADMIN_PASSWORD it
# replaces was: readable by anyone with access to the environment, and visible
# in the Vercel project settings.
ADMIN_USERS=""

# Shared single password, honoured only as a fallback when ADMIN_USERS is empty.
# Keeps a deploy from locking everyone out before ADMIN_USERS is set. Once
# ADMIN_USERS is in place this can be cleared.
ADMIN_PASSWORD=""

# Signs the session cookie. Must be set and must stay the same across deploys,
# or everyone gets logged out. Generate with: openssl rand -base64 32
SESSION_SECRET=""

# Supabase, used for every read and write in the admin.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=""
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=""